LGPL-2.1 obligations for the static link (Android)
--------------------------------------------------

On Android, libsndfile is linked statically into libyse.so, which makes
libyse.so a "work that uses the Library" combined with the Library (LGPL-2.1
section 6). To let recipients modify libsndfile and relink, every Android
archive (libyse-vX.Y.Z-android.tar.gz) ships, next to libyse.so:

  - licenses/libsndfile-COPYING.txt
        The full text of the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1,
        copied from the libsndfile source.
  - third_party/libsndfile-1.2.2-src.tar.gz
        The complete corresponding source of the libsndfile version that was
        linked (the upstream 1.2.2 tag, unmodified).

The rest of libyse.so is open source under the MIT License. Its complete source
for any release is the tagged commit vX.Y.Z of
https://github.com/yvanvds/yse-soundengine, and the source archives attached to
the same GitHub release. To relink with a modified libsndfile: build libsndfile
from the shipped (or your modified) source, then build libyse for Android from
the tagged YSE source as described in the repository README.md, with the FetchContent
declaration for "sndfile" in CMakeLists.txt pointed at your libsndfile tree
(for example -DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_SNDFILE=<path>).

The `yse.py package --platform android` step adds these files and refuses to
build an Android archive without them.


